module
public import Mathlib.Data.Fin.Basic

/-!
# Finite word data for the outer M₁₂ overlap extension

These are untrusted breadth-first word coordinates in the existing degree-24
permutations. `Coordinates` checks the overlap enumeration and multiplication;
the endpoint tables are supplied for the separate central-extension calculation.
The raw entries are natural numbers to keep elaboration and code generation
small. They imply no group identity before their companion kernel checks.

Source coordinates and ATLAS attribution: `Extension.Seeds`,
`Extension.FirstParabolic.Coordinates`, and `Extension.SecondParabolic.Coordinates`.
The deterministic producer is `source/generate.py` beside this module.
-/
@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Mathieu.M12ExceptionalExtension.OverlapExtensions.Data

